Potential automation:

- state tracking;
- timers;
- transport coordination;
- escalation.

Primary validation should show that staff currently have to:

- call the blood bank;
- call or find a courier;
- check whether a sample arrived;
- check whether compatibility testing is complete;
- chase issued blood;
- confirm bedside receipt;
- manually monitor urgent cases.

If those actions occur repeatedly, the 135-minute measured process becomes a strong workflow-automation candidate.

