Quantify only:

1. direct measured delay exposure;
2. stage-level delay;
3. urgent-case volume;
4. potential coordination effort;
5. sensitivity-based addressable time;
6. industry benchmark where useful.

Do **not** invent current Nayati staff minutes.

Do **not** assign monetary value to lives saved.

Do **not** assume all 135 minutes are automation-addressable.

The next checkpoint should determine whether the workflow has enough **human coordination exposure** to justify primary validation.

